<title>PHILIPPINES: BPI reaches foreign ownership limit.</title>
<headline>BPI reaches foreign ownership limit.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foreign portfolio investments in the Bank of the Philippine Islands have reached the maximum limit of 30 percent, a notice to the Philippine Stock Exchange said on Friday.</p>
<p>Analysts said this now prevents foreign portfolio investors from buying more BPI shares.</p>
<p>Philippine laws allow foreign investors to own up to 30 percent of a local bank. The level may be raised to 40 percent although it requires government approval.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 841-8937 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
